# Environment variables for portable data paths (P3).
#
# Configs may reference paths as ${VAR:-default}. When VAR is unset the default
# (the original absolute path) is used, so nothing changes out of the box; set a
# variable here (or export it) to relocate data without editing any config.
# The loader (src/config.py) expands ${VAR:-default} in all config string values.
#
# Copy to `.env` and edit, or `export` the ones you need before running.

# Root of the shared 1.5-degree KAI dataset (train/valid/test + stats/).
# Currently defaults to another user's home; set this to your own copy.
GW_KAI_1P5_ROOT=/lustre/home/mahmed/Hydro/kai_1p5_data

# Generic data root. Wired into the icomesh 2.5-degree experiment configs; the
# default is this machine's local copy of the 2.5/5.625-degree sets.
GW_DATA_ROOT=/home/amin/KAI_5

# --- Not yet wired into configs (documented pattern for future portability) ---
# Most 2.5-degree/5.625-degree configs still name /home/amin/KAI_5 literally. To
# make one portable, edit the config value to ${GW_ERA5_ROOT:-<absolute path>} and
# add the variable here.
# GW_ERA5_ROOT=/home/amin/KAI_5/era5_67
